# SRG-APP-000362-AU-000170  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to perform on-demand sorting of
# log records for events of interest based on the content of
# organization-defined audit fields within log records.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000362-AU-000170
group:           V-206495
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000158
control_rev5:    AU-7

contribution:    Sorting log records is a native Splunk search command and needs no
                 configuration, so the application's share is that the saved content the
                 organization sorts with exists in the product.

governs:         savedsearches.conf - Saved searches, scheduled reports and alerts.

check:           savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          savedsearches.conf [<stanza name>] search https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/savedsearches.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The organization's definition of which audit fields are of interest, which
                 the check text leaves organization-defined and no product setting supplies
external:        The field extractions the organization writes for its own sources
                 (props.conf EXTRACT- and REPORT- classes with transforms.conf), whose
                 content is specific to the data it collects

citation:        fields.conf [<field name>] INDEXED present is removed.
                 fields.conf.spec:89-94 makes it a boolean defaulting to false and states
                 that search-time extraction "accounts for the majority of fields", so the
                 condition failed twice over: present is satisfied by INDEXED = false and
                 therefore decides nothing, and requiring an index-time field declaration
                 before a record can be sorted fails the ordinary Splunk deployment, which
                 extracts at search time. Sorting itself needs no configuration, and which
                 fields are of interest is organization-defined, so no condition can carry
                 that part; it is recorded as an external dependency instead.
finding:         The product stores no saved search content for audit review, so the
                 organization's sorting of its audit fields is not expressed in the
                 application.
